=== Summary
tag::overview[]

You’ve seen a number of advanced tools that allow you to manipulate your checkpoints and staging area with surgical precision. When you notice an issue, you should now be able to easily figure out what decision introduced it, when, and by whom. 

You’ve also learned how to "pause" your creative flow with stashing and how to "curate" your history with rebasing. These tools transform Git from a simple file-tracker into a professional design-ops platform. 

In the next chapter, we’ll look at how Nora can **customize** Git to better handle the unique needs of a design team—from large binary assets to custom diff tools for visual files.
